--------------------------------------------------------------------------
DINOv3 weights policy (decision D1-a, design doc 28 section 6.1)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The DINOv3 backbone line is supported, but its pretrained weights are
published by Meta under the DINOv3 License (NOT Apache-2.0). This
framework never downloads those weights by default and does not
redistribute them: loading a pretrained DINOv3 checkpoint requires the
environment flag AUTOVISION_DINOV3_WEIGHTS=1, which asserts that the USER
has accepted Meta's DINOv3 License terms on their own account. Any model
trained from DINOv3-initial weights inherits those license obligations
(commercial use is permitted with redistribution notice: attach the
license and mark "Built with DINOv3"). Prefer the DINOv2 line when the
DINOv3 distillation gains are not required — but note DINOv2's HF
pretrained WEIGHTS are CC-BY-NC 4.0 (non-commercial; only its code is
Apache-2.0). The fully clean path for unrestricted use is DINOv2
``-notpretrained`` plus this framework's own self-supervised pretraining
on your data.

Runtime dependencies (not vendored) carry their own licenses; see
pyproject.toml. Optional integrations with AGPL-licensed or custom-licensed
software (e.g. Ultralytics, DINOv3 weights) are isolated behind optional
extras and runtime downloads and must never have source or weights copied
into this repository (docs/design/28-clean-provenance-refactor.md, rule R18).
